    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1126">

                <pb facs="0937" n="821" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg821"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/759.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-28T11:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 28, 1912—11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s telegram of July 26, 3 p.m. The persons mentioned by Senator Fall
                    have never been heard of at the Embassy, and it is believed that any American
                    consular officer in Mexico would be sure to report such indignities to the
                    Embassy and to the Department if known. The allegations of Senator Fall cannot
                    be investigated in the absence of reasonably specific data concerning time and
                    place. If there is any truth in the allegations at all it is more than likely
                    that they may be traced to retaliatory border raids between Americans and
                    Mexicans.</p>
                <p>No case presented to this Embassy, either directly by a claimant or through
                    official channels, has failed to be supported by the necessary diplomatic
                    representations to the Mexican Foreign Office. Senator Fall ought, it appears to
                    me, in the interest of the relations between the United States and Mexico, to be
                    answered by a senator conversant with the facts.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
